                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "22faf041-6322-3570-a939-93dbfb02018a",
                        "entry_id": "9a141428-533d-3520-b475-42a6ace84548",
                        "glosses": [
                            "юр. будучи свидетелем, давать ложные показания; совершать лжесвидетельство; быть лжесвидетелем"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "903d046f-7295-4f4a-853e-d5dd3400fd73",
                                "sense_id": "22faf041-6322-3570-a939-93dbfb02018a",
                                "text": "Он так трогательно просил о подписи, что подмахнули акт и такие пассажиры, которые не были очевидцами происшествия, а лжесвидетельствовали, так сказать, по добродушию, чтобы не обидеть отказом просящего человека."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc8059bd-b641-423c-a7a3-a061389ea9b0",
                                "sense_id": "22faf041-6322-3570-a939-93dbfb02018a",
                                "text": "И лжесвидетельствуют они не под пыткой, не под угрозой пытки, не под угрозой тюрьмы, ссылки или какого бы то ни было вида насилия, а находясь в полной безопасности, по любезному приглашению телефонного звонка."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cf35ef77-8398-42ca-9b94-20f07880aba7",
                        "source_entry_id": "9a141428-533d-3520-b475-42a6ace84548",
                        "source_sense_id": "22faf041-6322-3570-a939-93dbfb02018a",
                        "target_lang_word": "perjure",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "perjure",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "772728c1-db3e-372f-a2dc-783cbd6e27d8",
                                        "entry_id": "59f82e10-a2e5-3a19-a273-54525e522473",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To knowingly and willfully make a false statement of witness while in court."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "reflexive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f9a1b43-29bf-4876-8115-fb696c9dffb9",
                                                "sense_id": "772728c1-db3e-372f-a2dc-783cbd6e27d8",
                                                "text": "He perjured himself."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "924edc40-381a-3adb-8225-b7748ab8fdca",
                                        "entry_id": "59f82e10-a2e5-3a19-a273-54525e522473",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause to violate an oath or a vow; to cause to make oath knowingly to what is untrue; to make guilty of perjury; to forswear; to corrupt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "898599a8-87d2-47e9-922a-f84af72e5efd",
                                                "sense_id": "924edc40-381a-3adb-8225-b7748ab8fdca",
                                                "text": "Want will perjure the ne'er-touched vestal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b4c83c5-40c8-36a8-a9eb-a251be24805d",
                                        "entry_id": "59f82e10-a2e5-3a19-a273-54525e522473",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a false oath to; to deceive by oaths and protestations."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fcaf72e8-882f-4a6c-a8bf-e00c69160cb6",
                                                "sense_id": "7b4c83c5-40c8-36a8-a9eb-a251be24805d",
                                                "text": "And with a virgin innocence did pray / For me, that perjured her."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "perjure",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "803b5eec-8a71-3537-ba53-66e8d641d7b0",
                                        "entry_id": "4011ab9e-3a38-3ce0-aa25-c3a302d23d78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A perjured person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac2c8f64-220b-4f6d-b6b6-2bfefb8e4526",
                                                "sense_id": "803b5eec-8a71-3537-ba53-66e8d641d7b0",
                                                "text": "He comes in like a perjure, wearing papers"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e10a575f-9ae9-4e20-8c00-5377b8b9e7b6",
                        "source_entry_id": "9a141428-533d-3520-b475-42a6ace84548",
                        "source_sense_id": "22faf041-6322-3570-a939-93dbfb02018a",
                        "target_lang_word": "forswear",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "forswear",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da9beb5b-90fb-32bb-9165-0c6a7d123b38",
                                        "entry_id": "4e71ee3e-6d9f-3d7c-ba47-6760ba2c7fb6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To renounce or deny something, especially under oath."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e08829ba-0c85-4d06-8386-aaa85d22de09",
                                                "sense_id": "da9beb5b-90fb-32bb-9165-0c6a7d123b38",
                                                "text": "Like Innocence, and as serenely bold / As Truth, how loudly He forswears thy Gold!."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8225d906-e521-4ebc-aa21-07cd1cdacd34",
                                                "sense_id": "da9beb5b-90fb-32bb-9165-0c6a7d123b38",
                                                "text": "Never to woo her more; but do forswear her."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "154d2b39-6207-49af-8b73-11c607cfe07f",
                                                "sense_id": "da9beb5b-90fb-32bb-9165-0c6a7d123b38",
                                                "text": "We forswear allegiance and support for the Economic Freedom Fighters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebd7acd7-e4a4-473b-a1f5-b7f7ec5cb099",
                                                "sense_id": "da9beb5b-90fb-32bb-9165-0c6a7d123b38",
                                                "text": "Long since he had given up every intention of returning to civilization, and now he had decided to see no more his black friends of the Waziri. He had forsworn humanity forever. He had started life an ape—as an ape he would die."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41c5359f-de40-4657-b682-0af0c4786589",
                                                "sense_id": "da9beb5b-90fb-32bb-9165-0c6a7d123b38",
                                                "text": "Either forswear fucking others or the affair is over."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f077211-75e8-49fb-a123-9b638ce9b501",
                                                "sense_id": "da9beb5b-90fb-32bb-9165-0c6a7d123b38",
                                                "text": "The sheer unimaginableness of coming into her mouth — of coming into anything other than the air or a tissue or a dirty sock — was an allurement too stupendous for a novice to forswear."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d181466d-413e-475c-b797-bbe5ba7451bf",
                                                "sense_id": "da9beb5b-90fb-32bb-9165-0c6a7d123b38",
                                                "text": "Over the past two years, Silicon Valley’s leaders and investors — many of whom had once forsworn involvement in weapons and war — have plunged headfirst into the military industrial complex."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7cc9a494-1f20-3332-995c-eb68bd3a8bc9",
                                        "entry_id": "4e71ee3e-6d9f-3d7c-ba47-6760ba2c7fb6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To commit perjury; to break an oath."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "reflexive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
